{"slug": "la-zucca-magicas-orange-and-olive-salad", "nyt_id": 1014579, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014579-la-zucca-magicas-orange-and-olive-salad", "name": "La Zucca Magica’s Orange and Olive Salad", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "The combination of sweet, juicy, tart (and cold) orange and bitter, fatty, slightly warmer tapenade is fantastic. Don’t omit the fennel seeds, which add another dimension of flavor and texture — just super. And by all means use the common navel orange — it’s in season, and it seems, to me, just perfect.", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "PT20M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup good oil-cured black olives, pitted", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "good oil-cured black olives", "preparation": "pitted", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 teaspoon fresh thyme leaves (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fresh thyme leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup extra-virgin olive oil, more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": "more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 navel oranges, peeled and sliced into rounds", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "navel oranges", "preparation": "peeled and sliced into rounds", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Fennel seeds", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "fennel seeds", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a food processor, combine olives and thyme, if using, with a bit of olive oil. Pulse machine once or twice, then turn it on and add remaining olive oil rather quickly; you want this purée on the rough side. Thin with more olive oil if necessary. (You can refrigerate this for up to a month.)"}, {"position": 2, "text": "Layer 3 or 4 orange slices on each plate, drizzle with a little more olive oil, top with a tablespoon of olive purée and sprinkle with a few fennel seeds. Serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 233.5, "protein_g": 1.9, "carbohydrates_g": 20.6, "fat_g": 17.7, "saturated_fat_g": 2.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 250.3, "fiber_g": 4.4, "sugar_g": 11.9, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"], "diet": [], "course": ["salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "olive-oil", "orange", "quick"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 28}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-02-25", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:53:15Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lamb-and-couscous-salad-with-chickpeas-mint-and-feta", "nyt_id": 1013189, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013189-lamb-and-couscous-salad-with-chickpeas-mint-and-feta", "name": "Lamb and Couscous Salad With Chickpeas, Mint and Feta", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "PT15M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup dry couscous", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry couscous", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup golden raisins", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "golden raisins", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 ½ tablespoons freshly squeezed lemon juice, more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "freshly squeezed lemon juice", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 fat garlic clove, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "fat garlic clove", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon kosher salt, more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "6 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ pound cooked lamb, sliced into thin strips", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "cooked lamb", "preparation": "sliced into thin strips", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 15-ounce can chickpeas, drained", "group": null, "quantity": 16.0, "unit": null, "item": "ounce can chickpeas", "preparation": "drained", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 cup cherry tomatoes, quartered", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "cherry tomatoes", "preparation": "quartered", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "¼ pound feta cheese, crumbled into large chunks", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "lb", "item": "feta cheese", "preparation": "crumbled into large chunks", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "3 tablespoons chopped fresh mint", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh mint", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "3 scallions, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Combine the couscous and raisins in a large bowl. Pour 1 ¼ cups boiling water over the mixture. Cover and let stand 5 minutes; fluff with a fork."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a bowl, whisk together the lemon juice, cumin, garlic, salt and pepper. Whisk in the olive oil."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Add the lamb, chickpeas, tomatoes, feta, mint and scallions to the bowl of couscous. Pour the dressing over the mixture and toss well. Taste and add more lemon juice and salt if necessary."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 669.6666666666666, "protein_g": 14.7, "carbohydrates_g": 51.4, "fat_g": 45.9, "saturated_fat_g": 18.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 3.4, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 45.9, "sodium_mg": 530.7, "fiber_g": 7.2, "sugar_g": 11.9, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["couscous", "easy", "lamb", "quick", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 57}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-07-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:35:30Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lamb-chops-with-guajillo-chili-sauce-and-charro-beans", "nyt_id": 1014072, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014072-lamb-chops-with-guajillo-chili-sauce-and-charro-beans", "name": "Lamb Chops With Guajillo Chili Sauce and Charro Beans", "author": "Alex Witchel", "description": "Alex Witchel", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "PT1H30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "5 thyme sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": null, "item": "thyme sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "5 oregano sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": null, "item": "oregano sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "10 parsley sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "unit": null, "item": "parsley sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "10 cilantro sprigs", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "unit": null, "item": "cilantro sprigs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 garlic cloves", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "12 double-cut (2 ribs) baby lamb rib chops (about 10 ounces per serving)", "group": null, "quantity": 12.0, "unit": null, "item": "double-cut baby lamb rib chops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "5 guajillo chilies", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": null, "item": "guajillo chilies", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "3 garlic cloves", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "¼ cup chopped onion", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped onion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 whole plum tomato", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "whole plum tomato", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "4 cups beef or vegetable stock", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "beef or vegetable stock", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "1 tablespoon olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 19, "raw": "2 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 20, "raw": "½ cup finely diced red onion", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely diced red onion", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 21, "raw": "1 clove garlic, finely diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "finely diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 22, "raw": "1 small jalapeño, stemmed, seeded, and finely diced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "small jalapeño", "preparation": "stemmed, seeded, and finely diced", "optional": false}, {"position": 23, "raw": "2 15- to 16-ounce cans cannellini beans, rinsed and drained", "group": null, "quantity": 17.0, "unit": null, "item": "to 16-ounce cans cannellini beans", "preparation": "rinsed and drained", "optional": false}, {"position": 24, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 25, "raw": "freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "For the lamb: In a food processor, pulse thyme, oregano, parsley, cilantro and garlic cloves until finely chopped. Transfer to a large bowl, and whisk in wine and olive oil. Add chops and turn until thoroughly coated. Cover and refrigerate overnight."}, {"position": 2, "text": "For the sauce: Place a cast-iron or nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Place chilies in pan and turn until they are puffed and toasted; do not allow to burn or they will be bitter. Transfer to a medium saucepan. Toss 3 garlic cloves in skillet until lightly charred on all sides, then add to saucepan. Add onion to skillet, again toss until lightly charred, then add to saucepan. Add whole tomato to skillet, char until skin blisters and add to saucepan, along with stock. Bring to a boil, simmer for 5 minutes and allow to cool for 20 minutes. Pour sauce through a fine-mesh strainer into a bowl, reserving solids."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Remove chilies from strainer and discard any stems and seeds they contain. Place peppers in a food processor or blender with the rest of the reserved solids. Purée, adding just enough liquid to make a thick paste. In a small saucepan, heat 1 tablespoon olive oil until sizzling, then add chili paste. Stir for 1 minute, then gradually add reserved liquid (watch out for spattering) until it forms a thin sauce. Simmer 5 minutes. Season with salt and pepper to taste."}, {"position": 4, "text": "For the beans: In a large skillet over medium heat, heat olive oil until shimmering. Add red onion, garlic and jalapeño, and sauté until lightly browned. Add beans and toss until heated through. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Cover and keep warm."}, {"position": 5, "text": "To finish and serve: Prepare a grill or place a large skillet over medium-high heat. Remove chops from marinade, season with salt and pepper to taste, and cook on each side until medium-rare. Spoon sauce in a large circle on each of four plates, top with a serving of beans and arrange chops around the beans."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 756.75, "protein_g": 28.6, "carbohydrates_g": 61.4, "fat_g": 49.3, "saturated_fat_g": 14.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.8, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 53.9, "sodium_mg": 1597.0, "fiber_g": 15.2, "sugar_g": 3.7, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mexican"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course-sauces-and-gravies-steaks-and-chops"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["cannellini-bean", "guajillo-chile", "lamb-chop"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/29/dining/Lamb-Chops-With-Guajillo-Chili/Lamb-Chops-With-Guajillo-Chili-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/29/dining/Lamb-Chops-With-Guajillo-Chili/Lamb-Chops-With-Guajillo-Chili-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 45}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-03-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:49:09Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lamb-patties-with-mushroom-sauce", "nyt_id": 10070, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10070-lamb-patties-with-mushroom-sauce", "name": "Lamb Patties With Mushroom Sauce", "author": "Pierre Franey", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"total": "PT45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ¼ pounds ground lean lamb", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "unit": "lb", "item": "ground lean lamb", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ½ cups finely chopped onions", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped onions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 teaspoon finely chopped garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "finely chopped garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 teaspoon ground cumin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cumin", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped coriander or parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped coriander or parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup fine fresh bread crumbs", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "fine fresh bread crumbs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 egg, lightly beaten", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "egg", "preparation": "lightly beaten", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon butter", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "pound fresh mushrooms, thinly sliced, about 2 cups", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pound fresh mushrooms", "preparation": "thinly sliced, about 2 cups", "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons finely chopped shallots", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "finely chopped shallots", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "¼ cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "½ cup chopped peeled fresh tomatoes or canned crushed tomatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped peeled fresh tomatoes or canned crushed tomatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "¾ cup fresh or canned chicken broth", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "fresh or canned chicken broth", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "1 teaspoon chopped fresh tarragon or ½ teaspoon dried", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "chopped fresh tarragon or ½ teaspoon dried", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "2 teaspoons arrowroot or cornstarch", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "arrowroot or cornstarch", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "1 tablespoon water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the lamb in a mixing bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat two tablespoons of the oil in a small skillet and add the onions and garlic. Cook briefly, stirring, until wilted. Sprinkle with cumin and stir, blending well. Cool briefly."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Scrape the onion mixture into the lamb. Add the coriander, bread crumbs, egg, salt and pepper. Blend well with fingers and shape the mixture into 20 patties. Set aside."}, {"position": 4, "text": "For the mushroom sauce, heat the butter in a saucepan and add the mushrooms, shallots, salt and pepper. Cook over medium-high heat until all the moisture from the mushrooms has evaporated."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Add the wine and simmer briefly over high heat. Add the tomatoes, broth and tarragon. Cook about 5 minutes, stirring occasionally."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Blend the arrowroot with the water. Stir into the sauce and cook briefly."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Meanwhile, heat the remaining olive oil in a nonstick skillet large enough to hold the patties in one layer. Add the patties and turn them so they brown evenly, about 5 minutes. Drain the fat."}, {"position": 8, "text": "Add the patties to the sauce, cover and simmer about 10 minutes."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 1175.25, "protein_g": 17.4, "carbohydrates_g": 22.3, "fat_g": 114.4, "saturated_fat_g": 54.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.9, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 157.7, "sodium_mg": 1065.8, "fiber_g": 7.6, "sugar_g": 7.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["ground-lamb", "mushroom", "onion", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 29}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1990-04-04", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:29:36Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "large-white-bean-tuna-and-spinach-salad", "nyt_id": 1014616, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014616-large-white-bean-tuna-and-spinach-salad", "name": "Large White Bean, Tuna and Spinach Salad", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "You could use canned cannellini beans for this, but I love the size and texture of large white limas. I don’t soak limas because the skins tend to detach and the beans fall apart when you cook them. You want them intact for this, but you also need to make sure to cook them all the way through.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "PT2H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup large white lima beans", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "large white lima beans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 quart water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "quart", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 onion, cut in half", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "onion", "preparation": "cut in half", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 garlic cloves, crushed, plus 1 small garlic clove, minced or puréed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "crushed, plus 1 small garlic clove, minced or puréed", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 fresh sage leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "fresh sage leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 5-ounce can water-packed light tuna, drained", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": null, "item": "ounce can water-packed light tuna", "preparation": "drained", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 bunch spinach, stemmed, leaves washed and dried, or 1 6-ounce bag baby spinach", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "bunch", "item": "spinach", "preparation": "stemmed, leaves washed and dried, or 1 6-ounce bag baby spinach", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 tablespoon sherry vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 tablespoon fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ teaspoon Dijon mustard", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "dijon mustard", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "6 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 tablespoons finely chopped flat-leaf parsley and mint", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "finely chopped flat-leaf parsley and mint", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped chives", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped chives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "Sliced red onion and black olives", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "sliced red onion and black olives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Rinse the beans and combine with the water in a soup pot. Add the halved onion, the crushed garlic cloves, the bay leaf and the sage leaves. Bring to a gentle boil, add salt to taste, cover and boil very gently for 1 to 1 ½ hours, or until the beans are tender (sometimes they take longer, about 2 hours; it depends in part on the age of the beans). Remove from the heat. Set a colander over a bowl and drain the beans. Discard the bay leaf, onion, garlic cloves and sage. Some of the beans will have slipped out of their skins and fallen apart, but most should be intact. The broth can be used for a soup or pasta sauce."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, prepare the spinach and the dressing. Whisk together the vinegar, lemon juice, minced or puréed garlic, mustard, salt to taste and the olive oil."}, {"position": 3, "text": "In a large bowl, gently toss together the beans and the tuna. Don’t worry if some of the lima beans fall apart. Add the mint, half the chives and half the dressing and toss again. Season to taste with salt and pepper."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Toss the spinach with the remaining dressing. Line a platter or wide bowl with the spinach, top with the tuna, and sprinkle the remaining chives over the top. Garnish with red onions and black olives if desired, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 203.33333333333334, "protein_g": 8.9, "carbohydrates_g": 11.7, "fat_g": 14.3, "saturated_fat_g": 2.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 8.5, "sodium_mg": 731.4, "fiber_g": 3.5, "sugar_g": 1.7, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-salad"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["budget", "canned-tuna", "lima-bean", "spinach", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2013/03/19/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2013/03/19/science/22recipehealth/22recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 320}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2013-03-22", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:53:40Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "lavash-pizza-with-greens-baby-broccoli-and-mushrooms", "nyt_id": 1013321, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013321-lavash-pizza-with-greens-baby-broccoli-and-mushrooms", "name": "Lavash Pizza With Greens, Baby Broccoli and Mushrooms", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "I used a mix of packaged sturdy greens and baby broccoli for this substantial pizza, but you could also use rapini.", "servings": {"text": "2 servings", "min": 2, "max": 2, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "½ pound sturdy greens (kale or collards, or a mix)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "lb", "item": "sturdy greens (kale or collards", "preparation": "or a mix)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ pound baby broccoli tops", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "lb", "item": "baby broccoli tops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ pound mushrooms, sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "lb", "item": "mushrooms", "preparation": "sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 large garlic cloves, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic cloves", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon minced fresh rosemary (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "minced fresh rosemary", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup, tightly packed (2 ounces) grated Gruyère or fontina cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "½ cup, tightly packed (2 ounces) grated gruyère or fontina cheese", "preparation": "tightly packed (2 ounces) grated Gruyère or fontina cheese", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 9-by-12-inch lavash", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "unit": null, "item": "by-12-inch lavash", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil. Add the greens and the broccoli tops. Blanch for three minutes, then transfer to a bowl of ice water and drain. Squeeze out excess water and chop. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat the oven to 375 degrees, preferably with a pizza stone in it. Heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil over medium-high heat in a large, heavy nonstick pan. When the oil is hot, add the mushrooms. Cook, stirring or shaking often in the pan, for two minutes until they begin to soften. Add the garlic and rosemary, and salt and pepper to taste. Cook, stirring, for another 30 seconds to a minute until fragrant. Add the greens, stir together for a minute and remove from the heat. Season the mixture to taste with salt and pepper."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Place the lavash on a baking sheet, and sprinkle on the cheese in an even layer. Top with the greens. Drizzle on the remaining olive oil, and place the pizza in the oven. Bake 10 to 15 minutes, or until the edges of the lavash are crisp and browned. Remove from the heat, cut in half or into squares and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 408.0, "protein_g": 18.4, "carbohydrates_g": 31.3, "fat_g": 25.3, "saturated_fat_g": 8.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.5, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 38.3, "sodium_mg": 719.9, "fiber_g": 7.6, "sugar_g": 3.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["broccoli", "easy", "greens", "lavash", "quick", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/10/26/science/28recipehealth/28recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/10/26/science/28recipehealth/28recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 71}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-10-28", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:36:35Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "layered-vegetable-torte", "nyt_id": 1013213, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013213-layered-vegetable-torte", "name": "Layered Vegetable Torte", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "Getting this vegetable torte right takes a little time. You really must grill (or pan-grill) or roast all the vegetables well — they have to become quite tender — before assembling the torte. Ultimately, you want the vegetables to almost melt together. Grilling is the technique of choice because it gives the vegetables a hint of smokiness.", "servings": {"text": "4 to 6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "PT1H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 large eggplant, cut into ¼-inch slices", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large eggplant", "preparation": "cut into ¼-inch slices", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "4 medium zucchini or yellow squash, cut into ¼-inch slices", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium zucchini or yellow squash", "preparation": "cut into ¼-inch slices", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 portobello mushrooms, cut into ¼-inch slices", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "portobello mushrooms", "preparation": "cut into ¼-inch slices", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 red bell peppers, cored and cut into ¼-inch slices, optional", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "red bell peppers", "preparation": "cored and cut into ¼-inch slices, optional", "optional": true}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ cup extra virgin olive oil, or more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": "or more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 plum tomatoes, cut into ¼-inch slices", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "plum tomatoes", "preparation": "cut into ¼-inch slices", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons minced garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "minced garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "¼ cup chopped fresh basil leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped fresh basil leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "¼ cup freshly grated Parmesan", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "freshly grated parmesan", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "½ cup bread crumbs, preferably fresh", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "bread crumbs", "preparation": "preferably fresh", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 400 degrees. Put a grill pan over medium-high heat, or prepare a grill; the heat should be medium-high, and the rack about 4 inches from flame. Brush eggplant, zucchini, mushrooms and bell pepper, if using, lightly with half the oil and sprinkle with salt and pepper; if roasting, grease 2 baking sheets with oil. Roast or grill vegetables on both sides until soft."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Coat bottom and sides of 8-inch springform pan with oil. Layer a third of the eggplant slices into bottom of the pan, then layer in half the zucchini, mushrooms, bell pepper, if using, tomato, garlic and basil, sprinkling each layer with a bit of salt and pepper. Repeat layers until all vegetable are used. Press the top with a spatula or spoon to make the torte as compact as possible. Sprinkle top with Parmesan and bread crumbs, and drizzle with about 1 tablespoon oil."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Bake torte in oven until hot throughout and browned on top, about 30 minutes. Let sit for 5 minutes before removing outer ring of pan, then let cool for another 10 minutes before cutting into wedges."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 422.3333333333333, "protein_g": 9.3, "carbohydrates_g": 57.7, "fat_g": 20.9, "saturated_fat_g": 3.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.5, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 4.2, "sodium_mg": 1315.4, "fiber_g": 12.3, "sugar_g": 14.7, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["eggplant", "summer", "zucchini"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/08/05/multimedia/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/08/05/multimedia/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp-googleFourByThree.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/08/05/multimedia/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2024/08/05/multimedia/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp/Layered-Vegetable-Torterex-kmtp-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 1583}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-07-21", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:35:37Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
